This folder does not contain patient data. The dataset used in this study consists of retrospective clinical DXA scans and derived finite element models, which are subject to privacy and institutional data-sharing restrictions and cannot be redistributed publicly (see the manuscript's Data Availability Statement and Ethics Statement).

This README documents the expected data structure so that, once access has been granted (see below), the notebooks in ../notebooks/ can be run without modification.

How to request access

Requests to access the dataset underlying this study should be directed to the corresponding authors:

Abdollah Moslemi — abdollah.moslemi@upf.edu
Sikha Okkath Krishnanunni — sikha.okkath@upf.edu

Access is granted on a case-by-case basis in accordance with institutional ethics approval (CETIR Grup Mèdic Scientific Committee) and applicable data protection regulations. Requesters should expect to describe their intended use and, where required, execute a data use agreement with Pompeu Fabra University / CETIR Grup Mèdic.
Expected directory structure

Once data access has been granted, place the provided files into this folder following this structure:
data/
├── graphs/
│   ├── Co_GNN_Inps_0010007803_pyg.pkl
│   ├── Co_GNN_Inps_0027027422_pyg.pkl
│   ├── Fx_GNN_Inps_0013900409_pyg.pkl
│   ├── ...                              # 128 total: 64 "Co_" (control), 64 "Fx_" (fracture)
├── stress_labels/
│   ├── 0010007803.csv
│   ├── 0027027422.csv
│   ├── 0013900409.csv
│   ├── ...                              # 128 total, one CSV per patient, matched by numeric ID
└── splits/
    └── verified_test_patient_ids.txt    # the 20 patient IDs used as the held-out test set
                                          # in the manuscript (seed=42, patient-level split)
